SET ECHO OFF
STOP_ON_ERROR OFF
ECHO === FOREIGN TABLE LOCK PROBE, PART 1 of 2 -- build the fixture ===
ECHO
ECHO Part 1 makes one table and closes it. The harness then hand-writes a
ECHO <dbf>.lock owned by a DIFFERENT, LIVE process. Part 2 tries to grow and
ECHO change the table through four doors and reports which the fence stops.
ECHO
ECHO WHY THIS MEASURES A CROSS-PROCESS QUESTION IN ONE PROCESS. The fence is a
ECHO lock FILE whose owner token is host:pid:ms, minted once per process
ECHO (xbase_locks.cpp:41). "Another process" means nothing more than an owner
ECHO string that is not ours over a pid that is alive -- create_or_validate_owned
ECHO removes a lock only when the pid is PROVABLY dead, and fails closed
ECHO otherwise. A hand-written lock carrying the harness's own live pid is
ECHO therefore indistinguishable from a second engine holding the table.
SET PATH DBF DBF/SANDBOX
ERASE LOCKP CONFIRM
CREATE X64 LOCKP (ID C(4), TAG C(12))
USE LOCKP
INSERT (ID,TAG) VALUES ("S1","SEED1")
INSERT (ID,TAG) VALUES ("S2","SEED2")
ECHO seeded, expect 2:
COUNT
USE
ECHO === part 1 done ===
